  "measurement_scope": "Windows original Typora 1.14.10 on a private desktop, software rendering. Each performance scene posts two bounded 100-step HWND drags. Received trusted events may be coalesced. Timing covers renderer input receipt to changed native content geometry on rAF; gaps include settling/idle. Reference and final performance phases are identical; later source/split diagnostics were extended. Counts distinguish fences from actually instantiated CodeMirror editors. User text is copied only to ignored fixtures.",
  "intermediate_findings": [
    "Whole-window notifications removed first; body geometry and block consumers were then scoped.",
    "Source adapters retaining separate anchors still drifted. Consolidated font/container ownership and measured the retained virtual line before restoring its offset.",
    "An initial split assertion incorrectly compared native content to a moved preview leaf. Corrected the fixture to resize the actual native owning group and its adjacent divider.",
    "One UI complexity assertion read its counter after asynchronous layout; captured the measurement synchronously. A function-valued IPC test return was changed to void."
  ],
